WEBVTT

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.546
[Buck laughs]

00:00:06.631 --> 00:00:10.009
You picked a bad time
for a tropical vacation, lads.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:13.096
A dino named Orson
just escaped from exile.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.224
And he's jonesing to rule the Lost World.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:18.017
Now he's got a couple of raptors.

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:21.479
And if he succeeds,
no mammal will be safe.

00:00:21.562 --> 00:00:24.065
Whoa! Well, it's a good thing
I'm not a mammal.

00:00:24.148 --> 00:00:25.900
-You are a mammal.
-Sorry, bro.

00:00:25.983 --> 00:00:27.985
Looks like life dealt you a bad hand.

00:00:28.069 --> 00:00:29.153
You're a mammal too.

00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:30.321
That's impossible.

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:32.949
What are the odds of two possums
being mammals?

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:36.911
Well, they're the same odds
that you'll both be a raptor's brunch

00:00:36.994 --> 00:00:38.788
if I don't get you out of here.

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.249
[pterodactyl chirps, squawks]

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:48.214
Got to feed Penelope.

00:00:50.008 --> 00:00:52.927
She needs gas,
and these berries will give it to her.

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:56.305
Back off, Brenda. They're friends of mine.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.433
-[muffled groaning]
-[Buck] Brenda.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.893
Spit.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.063
Spit.

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:06.024
[muffled screaming]

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.235
So far, best day ever!

00:01:09.318 --> 00:01:12.155
Now, tell me, what brings you two
to my world?

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.322
We moved out.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.700
Yeah, we're mature now.

00:01:15.783 --> 00:01:17.076
Really?

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.829
Well, at first, Ellie was all…
[imitates Ellie] "Yada yada yada."

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.373
And then Manny was like…
[imitates Manny] "Blah, blah, blah."

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:24.459
Yeah, that does sound like him.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:26.961
And Diego was all-- [growling]

00:01:27.045 --> 00:01:28.421
I mean, you know how he is.

00:01:28.504 --> 00:01:30.590
And then Ellie said, "I don't like it,

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:33.217
but I suppose it's time.
Good luck out there."

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:36.804
Then she hugged us, Sid scratched himself,
and bingo bongo in the Congo, we're here!

00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:39.891
You're telling me Ellie
gave her okey dokey

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:42.226
to this little artichokey
of a mission here?

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.811
Oh, yeah. Totally.

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:45.104
-[gasps]
-Hmm?

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:47.273
Okay, okay. We snuck out.

00:01:47.357 --> 00:01:48.649
Ow!

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.234
You try to survive that look.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.613
[gulps]

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:57.075
I admit it! Whatever it is! [panting]

00:01:57.158 --> 00:01:59.369
I've got to take you back home, fellas.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.454
I'm the only one that can stop Orson,

00:02:01.537 --> 00:02:04.707
but I won't be able to do that
if I have you two to look after.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.125
But-but-but-but, Buck,

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:09.796
we came here to live a life
of adventure, like you.

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:12.548
You boys are nature's least likely
to survive.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.259
And this is its most dangerous place.

00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:17.762
Wow. Talk about a perfect match.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.523
I'll be back in a minute, girl.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.275
[Crash] Buck, don't send us back.

00:02:31.859 --> 00:02:33.820
[Eddie] Yeah, yeah, yeah.
We wanna hang here with you.

00:02:33.903 --> 00:02:35.446
[Crash] Please. We're independent.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:36.781
Both of us.

00:02:36.864 --> 00:02:37.907
Together.

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:41.828
This boulder's not supposed to be here.
How did it get here?

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:43.705
[Orson] Hmm… How do you think?

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:44.956
Well, how should I know?

00:02:45.039 --> 00:02:49.335
[Orson] Unbelievable.
Your cluelessness is truly breathtaking.

00:02:49.419 --> 00:02:52.171
Don't you take that tone with me, Rocky.

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:54.632
Now I insist you roll away at once.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:57.635
Uh, I don't think
it's the boulder talking.

00:02:57.719 --> 00:03:00.513
Well, not anymore.
I obviously intimidated him.

00:03:00.596 --> 00:03:03.933
Seems like Mr. Boulder here
is all growl and no gravel.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:06.561
Wow. Okay, enough. [laughs]

00:03:06.644 --> 00:03:08.146
I can't do this anymore.

00:03:08.229 --> 00:03:11.149
Hey, I'm over here,
you soon-to-be ex-weasel.

00:03:12.108 --> 00:03:14.569
Look at me.
Look at me with your dumb little eye.

00:03:16.487 --> 00:03:17.655
Orson.

00:03:18.906 --> 00:03:20.324
Buck.

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:21.534
Eddie.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.995
Crash.

00:03:24.078 --> 00:03:26.789
I heard you'd returned. But how?

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.334
Nobody escapes from Lava Island.

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:32.545
Well, not everyone
has my colossal intellect.

00:03:32.628 --> 00:03:36.341
Which is dwarfed only by your ego
and insecurity.

00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:38.343
Why'd you seal the exit, Orson?

00:03:38.926 --> 00:03:41.888
Oh, no reason. Just to keep
filthy animals like you

00:03:41.971 --> 00:03:47.101
from coming in and infecting our ecosystem
with your fur and warm blood.

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:49.520
Lost World for lost species!

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:52.190
Dinos rule… [chuckles] …mammals drool.

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:54.233
It's true. You do.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:57.153
Wait a minute. Dinos don't talk.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:59.614
They just grunt and roar like nincompoops.

00:03:59.697 --> 00:04:02.450
That's good. Hey, that's funny.
That's really funny.

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:04.327
Dinos have tiny brains.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.496
Like I haven't heard that a million times.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.332
Does this brain look tiny to you?

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.626
Holy moly, that's huge!

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:13.795
Seriously. That thing's a planet.

00:04:13.878 --> 00:04:16.881
I'm surprised there isn't
a little moon going around it. [laughs]

00:04:16.964 --> 00:04:20.468
That kind of reaction used to hurt.
I thought I was a freak.

00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:25.807
Then I realized that my massive brain
made me the smartest creature alive!

00:04:26.724 --> 00:04:29.560
But you know the best part?
The joke's on you.

00:04:29.644 --> 00:04:32.397
My brain, the thing
that everyone ridiculed,

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:35.274
is the one thing
that's gonna get me my revenge.

00:04:35.983 --> 00:04:38.277
I'll rule everyone under the ice!

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.573
Not even you can stop me this time,
Buckmeinster.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:44.992
[gasps]

00:04:45.076 --> 00:04:46.619
It's Buckminster.

00:04:46.703 --> 00:04:48.204
[screams]

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:50.540
Though most call me Buck.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.834
"Buckmeinster" is not even a name.

00:04:52.917 --> 00:04:56.754
That's like me calling you "Shmorson."

00:04:57.338 --> 00:05:01.676
Whatever, Bucky. Now that I've got
some muscle behind me,

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:04.429
it's a whole new ball game.

00:05:05.555 --> 00:05:07.432
[gasps] There's gonna be a ball game?

00:05:07.515 --> 00:05:10.351
[groans] Check it out.

00:05:10.852 --> 00:05:12.687
[gasps, screams]

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.022
[both groan]

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:17.775
[scoffs]
Well, look. They've gone and died.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:20.028
No one wants to eat dead possums.

00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:22.655
It's too chewy.
It's like eating hairy gum.

00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:23.740
Okay.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.408
I can totally see you're breathing.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.786
[Orson] Look, look-- Right there.
Look, even these morons can see it.

00:05:30.538 --> 00:05:33.124
Time for a possum picnic!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.418
Oh!

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:40.548
Oh!

00:05:42.216 --> 00:05:45.345
Until our next tango, mi iguana gigante.

